    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1284">

                <pb facs="1168" n="910" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg910"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 138/142</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-22T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 22, 1915, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>138. Ambassador London telegraphs 17th James Cook Trumbull of Rockefeller
                    Foundation experienced trouble in England because he carried emergency passport
                    issued by yourself on form printed in Switzerland instead of regular form to
                    take the place of regular passport issued by Department March 16. Apparently you
                    took up Department passport because French consuls are unwilling to visa
                    passports of persons who have been in Germany, Austria or Turkey. Department
                    does not consider action taken in Trumbull case advisable. It is believed that
                    if this case had been fully explained to French Consulate or Legation visa of
                    Department passport might have been obtained.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
